let's talk about all of these foreign  policy challenges with Brian Hook senior  policy adviser to the Secretary of State  he joins us tonight from Washington  Brian thanks for being here thanks Brian  good to be with you let's start with  Iran and what Secretary Pompeo said  today how realistic does the secretary  does the State Department does the  administration believe that these 12  stipulations will actually be agreed to  eventually by Iran the list of  requirements that secretary Pompeo  called out today in this speech on Iran  is a very reasonable and realistic list  in fact if you go through the list  it focuses on things like Iran's nuclear  weapons program its support for  terrorism its Foreign Wars that it funds  around the Middle East its violation of  Human Rights  all of these are positions that the  United States and its European allies  have held at one time or another and so  this is the kind of new approach that we  are taking to create a new security  architecture in the context of the  totality of Iran's threats you know  here's someone who negotiated before  former ambassador Wendy Sherman talking  about this I think that Pompeo gave us a  wish list today and it's a wish list  probably everybody could agree to but  you can't get it all at once because  then you're negotiating against yourself  as one is traded off against the other  you respond to that  well I think that's a very defeatist  attitude and I think that when it comes  to addressing the full range of Iranian  threats we do need to take a  comprehensive and very ambitious  approach in the speech the Secretary of  Pompeo delivered today does exactly that  yeah on the tweets coming from the  Iranians at the end of it it references  that Iran is still working with European  partners to continue the jcpoa the Iran  nuclear agreement that the u.s. pulled  out of how much of a problem is that  going forward and how do you calculate  that in I think that the United States  and its European 