 Korea as we sit  here today the  what do you think the likelihood is that  the June 12th summit moves forward  between President Trump and Kim jong-il  well secretary Pompeo has now made two  trips to North Korea to try to set the  table for a successful meeting in  Singapore on June 12th these sorts of  things take twists and turns that's not  uncommon with North Korea and so all we  can do is try to be in a state of  readiness and to do what we can so that  we can have a very good discussion about  as president Trump has talked about a  very bright future for the North Korean  people if there is if the regime is  willing to denuclearize and last thing  for the people up on Capitol Hill people  who are skeptical of how this is all  coming together what do you tell them  that the administration the president is  not going to give the store away or is  not going to get played by either in  North Korea or China in negotiations  ongoing I think the president is coming  in from a position of great strength he  has assembled the largest sanctions  campaign against North Korea in history  and so he's in a very good position  whether the talks happen or not whether  the talks go well or poorly the global  maximum pressure campaign is going to  continue until we achieve our national  security objectives  Brian Hooke director of policy of the  State Department  thanks for being here love to have you  back okay thanks Brett
 

